<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela bolivar softens for fourth straight day.</title>
<headline>Venezuela bolivar softens for fourth straight day.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Venezuelan bolivar softened on Tuesday for the fourth consecutive session, closing at 475.00/476.00 per dollar in light trading, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The central bank intervened very little, letting the price rise on corporate dollar demand,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>The bolivar closed Monday at 473.75/475.00 per dollar.</p>
<p>((-- Oscar Galvis, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
